@startuml 05-state-machine-trip
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
title State machine — Trip lifecycle and GPS signal state

[*] --> Active : startTrip(route, shuttle)\n[route in service, shuttle and driver free]

state Active {
  [*] --> AwaitingFix
  AwaitingFix : do / show "waiting for first GPS position"
  Live : entry / show live ETAs
  Live : fix accepted / update position, speed, ETAs
  Stale : do / show ETAs as approximate (~)
  Lost : do / hide ETAs, show "last seen"

  AwaitingFix --> Live : fix accepted
  AwaitingFix --> Lost : after(60 s)
  Live --> Stale : after(20 s) [no newer fix]
  Live --> Lost : after(60 s)\n[e.g. an old offline backlog,\nor after a server restart]
  Stale --> Lost : after(60 s since last fix)
  Stale --> Live : fix accepted
  Lost --> Live : fix accepted
}

Active --> Completed : endTrip() [by its driver]
Active --> Terminated : terminate(reason) [by office]
Active --> Terminated : after(30 min without an accepted fix)\n/ endReason = NO_SIGNAL_TIMEOUT
Completed --> [*]
Terminated --> [*]

note right of Active
  Ages are measured from the newest
  accepted fix (server-corrected time),
  or from the trip start if there is none.
  Thresholds are configurable
  (STALE_AFTER_SECONDS, LOST_AFTER_SECONDS,
  ABANDON_AFTER_MINUTES). A trip recovered
  after a restart re-enters Live and is then
  re-evaluated on the next tick.
end note
@enduml
